{"id":"word:hebrew:H1732","type":"word","title":"דָּוִד","subtitle":"H1732 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"David , the youngest son of Jesse","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to דָּוִד (H1732) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-pr-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 1075 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"דָּוִד (Dâvid) means David , the youngest son of Jesse First listed occurrence: 1Chr 2 15."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"דָּוִד","transliteration":"Dâvid","pronunciation":"daw-veed'","strong":"H1732","lemmaId":"hebrew:H1732","partOfSpeech":"n-pr-m","forms":["דָּוִ֔ד","דָּוִד֙","דָּוִ֖ד","דָּוִ֑ד","דָּוִ֗ד"],"morphs":[["HNp",847],["HR/Np",183],["HC/Np",44],["HC/R/Np",1]]},"definitions":{"short":"David , the youngest son of Jesse","usage":"David.","full":"H1732. David דָּוִיד דָּוִד, 1066 proper name, masculine David , son of יִשַׂי , king of Israel, whose dynasty remained on the throne of Jerusalem till the Babylonian exile (compare 2Sam 7:11-15 etc.) ( beloved one ? compare Ba NB 189 ; according to Sayce Modern Rev. 1884, 158 ff.; Rel. Babylonian 53, 56 f. originally Dodo , title of sun-god worshipped in Israel compare דודה name of divinity among east Jordan Israelites MI 12 ) — דָּוִד always Ruth, Samuel, Kings (except 1Kin 3:14 ; 11:4 , 36 ) Psalms, Proverbs, Ecclesiastes, Isaiah, Jeremiah; also 1Chr 13:6 ; Ezek 34:24 ; 37:24-25 , (c. 790 t.); דָּוִיד always Zechariah, Chronicles (except 1Chr 13:6 ), Ezra, Nehemiah; also Amos 6:5 (where gloss according to Peters Hebraica. Apr. 1886, p. 175 ) 9:11 ; Hosea 3:5 ; Ezek 34:23 ; 1Kin 3:14 ; 11:4 , 36 ; Song 4:4 (c. 276 t.); — first named 1Sam 16:13 ; compare also Ruth 4:17 , 22 ; 2Sam 1:1 +, 1Kin 1:1 +, 2:1 +, etc. (see above); in titles of Psalm 3-9, 11-32, 34-41, 51-65, 68-70, 86, 101, 103, 108-110, 122, 124, 131, 133, 138-145 (73 in all); also in Psalm 18:51 (= 2Sam 22:51 ); 2Sam 72:20; 2Sam 89:36; 2Sam 89:50; 2Sam 122:5; 2Sam 132:1132:11; 132:17; ׳ד עַבְדִּי ( ׳י speaks) 3:18 ; 7:5 , 8 = 1Chr 17:4 , 7 compare 17:26 = 17:24 , also 1Kin 8:24-25 , 26 , 66 2Chr 6:15 ; 6:16 ; 6:17 ; 6:42 , 1Kin 11:13 ; 11:32 ; 11:34 ; 11:36 ; 11:38 ; 14:8 ; 2Kin 8:19 ; 19:34 = Isa 37:35 ; 2Kin 20:6 ; compare further Psa 18:1 ; 36:1 (both titles compare above) 78:70 ; 89:4 ; 89:21 ; 132:10 ; 144:10 ; Jer 33:21-22 , 26 ; so also as represented in coming (Messianic) ruler Ezek 34:23-24 , 37:24-25 , compare Hosea 3:5 ; Jer 30:9 (see עֶבֶד ). Phrases are: a. ד ׳עִיר (according to Sayce Mod.Rev.l.c. originally city of god Dod [o] ) = stronghold or citadel of Zion, 2Sam 5:7 , 9 = 1Chr 11:5 , 7 ; 2Sam 6:10 , 12 , 16 = 1Chr 13:13 ; 15:1 , 29 , compare Isa 22:9 ; especially of burial of kings 1Kin 2:10 ; 3:1 ; 8:1 2Chr 5:2 ; 1Kin 9:24 2Chr 8:11 ; 1Kin 11:27 11:43 2Chr 9:31 ; 1Kin 14:13 ; 15:8 2Chr 12:16 ; 2 Chronicles 13:23; 1Kin 15:24 2Chr 9:31 ; 1Kin 14:31 ; 15:8 2Chr 12:16 ; 2 Chronicles 13:23; 1Kin 15:24 2Chr 16:14 ; 1Kin 22:50 2Chr 21:1 ; 2Kin 8:24 2Chr 21:20 ; 2Kin 9:28 ; 2 Kings 12:22 2Chr 24:25 ; 2Kin 14:20 ; 15:7 , 15:38 2Chr 27:9 ; 2Kin 16:20 ; burial of Jehoiada 2Chr 24:16 ; further 32:5 , 30 ; 33:14 ; Neh 12:37 ; compare also ד חָנָה ׳קִרְיַת Isa 29:1 . b. ד ׳בֵּית 2Sam 3:1 , 6 + (compare בַּיִת 5c . c. ד ׳אֹהֶל Isa 16:5 (compare אֹהֶל 2 ). d. ד ׳סֻכַּת Amos 9:11 (compare סֻכָּה below סכך ). e. ד ׳כִּסֵּא 2Sam 3:10 compare 1Kin 1:37 ; 2:12 , 24 , 45 ; Isa 9:6 ; Jer 17:25 ; 22:2 , 30 ; 29:16 ; 36:30 ; compare 13:13 ; 22:4 , (compare also כִּסֵּא ). f. ד ׳קִבְרֵי Neh 3:16 compare 2Chr 32:33 בְנֵידֿ ׳קִבְרֵי (compare קֶבֶר ). g. ד ׳מִגְדַּל Song 4:4 . h. ד ׳כְּלֵישִֿׁיר האלהים אישׁ Neh 12:36 . i. ד ׳אֱלֹהֵי 2Kin 20:5 + (compare אֱלֹהִים 4b ). j. ד ׳חַסְדֵי 2Chr 6:42 ; Isa 55:3 (compare 2Sam 7:15 ; 1Kin 3:6 ; Psa 89:50 ; 2Chr 1:8 etc.). — (On text note the following: — דָּוִד 1Sam 30:20 a strike out ᵑ7 ᵐ5 We Dr; 2Sam 3:5 read probably name of a former husband of Eglah We Dr; 13:39 read רוּחַ We p.223 Dr; 2 Samuel 19:44 read בְּכוֺר (for בדוד ) ᵐ5 The We Dr; insert דָּוִד 9:11 ; 15:32 & 24:15 ᵐ5 We Dr; in 1Chr 18:12 ; Psa 60:1 אבשׁי & יואב are less original than דָּוִד 2Sam 8:13 We Dr).","rootNote":"rarely (fully); דָּוִיד ; from the same as 1730 ; loving ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 2 15","keyReferences":["1Chr 2 15","1Chr 3 1","1Chr 3 9","1Chr 4 31","1Chr 6 16","1Chr 7 2","1Chr 9 22","1Chr 10 14"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":1075,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Chr 2 15","book":"1Chr","chapter":2,"verse":15,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"דָּוִ֖יד","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNp"},{"reference":"1Chr 3 1","book":"1Chr","chapter":3,"verse":1,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"דָויִ֔ד","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNp"},{"reference":"1Chr 3 9","book":"1Chr","chapter":3,"verse":9,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"דָוִ֑יד","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNp"},{"reference":"1Chr 4 31","book":"1Chr","chapter":4,"verse":31,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"דָּוִֽיד","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNp"},{"reference":"1Chr 6 16","book":"1Chr","chapter":6,"verse":16,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"דָּוִ֛יד","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNp"},{"reference":"1Chr 7 2","book":"1Chr","chapter":7,"verse":2,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"דָוִ֔יד","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNp"},{"reference":"1Chr 9 22","book":"1Chr","chapter":9,"verse":22,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"דָּוִ֛יד","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNp"},{"reference":"1Chr 10 14","book":"1Chr","chapter":10,"verse":14,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"לְ/דָוִ֖יד","source":"hebrew","morph":"HR/Np"},{"reference":"1Chr 11 1","book":"1Chr","chapter":11,"verse":1,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"דָּוִ֖יד","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNp"},{"reference":"1Chr 11 3","book":"1Chr","chapter":11,"verse":3,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"דָּוִ֥יד","source":"hebrew","morph":"HNp"},{"reference":"1Chr 11 3","book":